cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Sleepability Pass: a C-side CanSleep summary for the Linux kernel"
abstract: >-
  A standalone out-of-tree LLVM module pass that computes, per function, whether
  it may sleep (the kernel CanSleep property) by propagating reachability to
  blocking primitives bottom-up over the call graph's strongly connected
  components, with argument-sensitive handling of kmalloc gfp flags. The C-side
  (callee-summary) half of a proposed cross-language sleepability checker (CLSC).
